==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|rēctō|lang=la}} {{term|folium|foliō|on the right leaf, on the right page|lang=la}}, the [[ablative]] of the Latin {{term|rēctus||right|lang=la}}. Confer {{term|versus||turned|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɹɛk.toʊ/}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia|Recto and verso}}
{{en-noun}}

# The front side of a flat object which is to be examined visually, as for reading, such as a sheet or a leaf or a [[coin]] or a [[medal]].
# Therefore, {{context|printing|lang=en}} the [[right-hand]] [[page]] of a [[book]] of a script which reads from left to right, usually having an odd page number.
# {{context|legal|lang=en}} A [[writ]] of [[right]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|front side of a flat object}} [[front#Noun|front]]

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|front side of a flat object}} [[verso]], [[flipside]]

